ai-safety-comment-validation.prompt:
You are auditing a Rust // SAFETY comment on an unsafe block in {{filename}}.

A valid SAFETY comment names the concrete invariants, preconditions, or ownership guarantees that make the unsafe operations sound. An invalid one is generic, circular, or unrelated to the actual unsafe operations ("this is safe", "we checked", "trust me").

Context: {{rule_context}}

Code (SAFETY comment plus surrounding lines):
{{code}}

Decide whether the SAFETY comment fails to justify the unsafe block. Set is_issue to true only when the justification is missing, generic, or does not correspond to the unsafe operations shown.

ai-doc-comment-quality.prompt:
You are auditing a Rust doc-comment on a public item in {{filename}}.

A useful doc-comment adds information the reader cannot recover from the item name and signature: what it returns in edge cases, when it errors or panics, invariants, units, or non-obvious behavior. A low-value doc-comment merely restates the name.

Context: {{rule_context}}

Code (doc-comment plus the item it documents):
{{code}}

Decide whether the doc-comment only paraphrases the name and signature. Set is_issue to true only when it adds no information beyond what the name already conveys.
